WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:08.500
In 2007, The Big Bang Theory debuted on CBS.
But the sitcom didn’t explode in popularity

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.800
until reruns hit syndication. Since then,
its season premieres have routinely ranked

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.650
near the top of network TV ratings, and reruns
dominate the list of most-watched cable shows.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:23.029
But for any shows this huge, there are bound
to be some big bangs behind the scenes, too…

00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:25.470
The Pilot Reconceptualization

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.380
The show that's aired for nearly a decade
is very different from the original pilot.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.890
Jim Parsons as Sheldon was originally a horndog.
His character was changed to someone mystified

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:34.540
by romance:

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:38.840
"I have seen 6 women naked. Some of them weren't
even relatives."

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.640
Kaley Cuoco’s Penny was also absent. Instead,
the attractive neighbor was the unfriendly

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:48.470
Katie, played by Amanda Walsh. Johnny Galecki
as Leonard wore suits instead of hoodies.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:52.840
And there was one other change: the theme
song was Thomas Dolby's "She Blinded Me With

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:57.190
Science." CBS passed, but asked creators Chuck
Lorre and Bill Prady to rework the show and

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:01.370
submit another pilot. They did, adding an
original theme by Barenaked Ladies, and made

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.040
it to air in 2007.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.900
The Bernadette Vocalization

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:08.830
Bernadette's mousy, high-pitched voice, and
loud moments of screaming rage, don't come

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.340
naturally to actress Melissa Rauch.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.560
"She said I'm a wonderful girl and that you're
lucky to have me."

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:14.880
"Where are you going?"

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.820
"To the toilet, is that ok with you?!"

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:21.250
Although she doesn't sound like Bernadette
in real life, Rauch took her inspiration from

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:23.070
a source close to home: her own mother:

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:27.440
"They'll say things like, 'I went to the grocery
store and I had to return something and they

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:31.080
sent me to three different counters. It was
a real circle jerk!'"

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.110
The Paycheck Extortion

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:37.370
In 2014, production of the show's eighth season
was delayed due to contract re-negotiations

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:41.670
between the cast and Warner Brothers. Ultimately,
CBS renewed the show for an unprecedented

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:46.979
three seasons, keeping it on the air through
2017. Jim Parsons, Johnny Galecki, and Kaley

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:50.740
Cuoco each secured a salary of $1 million
per episode.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:55.140
Meanwhile, Simon Helberg and Kunal Nayyar
re-negotiated their new contracts collectively,

00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:00.110
ending up with salaries of around $750,000
per episode. A settlement was reached the

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:03.880
day before their old contracts expired, but
the duo would've reportedly been written out

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:06.340
of the show if they hadn't accepted the deal.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.420
The Relationship Obfuscation

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.940
Kaley Cuoco has often appeared in tabloids
due to her brief marriage to tennis player

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:16.630
Ryan Sweeting. Still, she avoided the spotlight
during her previous relationship, even though

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:21.920
it was with a noteworthy co-star. Cuoco and
Johnny Galecki dated from 2007 to 2009 and

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.170
kept it a secret from not only the media,
but from the Big Bang cast and crew:

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:29.790
"We totally fell for each other and just really
wanted to keep it as close to ourselves as

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.150
possible, and we had an amazing relationship."

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.560
The Mayim Bialik Manifestation

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.500
In the 2008 episode "The Bat Jar Conjecture,"
Sheldon quits the group's physics bowl team.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.760
Raj aims high in his suggestion for a replacement:

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:45.500
"You know who is apparently very smart is
the girl who played TV's Blossom. She got

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.849
a PHD in neuroscience or something."

00:02:48.849 --> 00:02:52.830
"Raj, we're not getting TV's Blossom to join
our Physics Bowl team."

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:57.489
That actress is Mayim Bialik, who later joined
the cast as Amy Farrah Fowler. Also under

00:02:57.489 --> 00:03:01.379
consideration for the role was actress and
musician Kate Micucci. She was edged out for

00:03:01.379 --> 00:03:05.160
the part, but producers liked her so much
that they wrote her in anyhow, as Lucy, the

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.020
extremely introverted woman Raj briefly dates.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.730
The Soft Kitty Misappropriation

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:18.470
"Soft kitty warm kitty little ball of fur.
See that's where you would come in."

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:23.129
Co-creator Bill Prady says he heard Sheldon's
special calm-down song at his daughter's preschool.

00:03:23.129 --> 00:03:26.720
Assuming it was public domain, he added it
to the show, where it's been used multiple

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.739
times and on Big Bang merchandise.

00:03:28.739 --> 00:03:34.200
In 2015, however, the family of a teacher
named Edith Newlin sued CBS. Allegedly, the

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.810
show lifted lyrics from Newlin's 1937 song
"Warm Kitty." The main difference? The original

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:42.800
1937 lyrics switch the first two lines from
the song we now know and love. This whole

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.140
thing could make for one rich kitty...

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:51.720
"Happy kitty sleepy kitty purrr purrr purrrrr!"

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.870
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.690
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know what you’ve heard about The Big

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:58.410
Bang Theory...

